# Tierra Andina API — request examples.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Every error response has the shape { "error": { "code", "message", "details"? } }.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### Liveness — 200 { "ok": true, "version": "0.1.0" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Database check — 200 { "ok": true, "db": "up" } | 503 DB_UNAVAILABLE
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/db

### Unknown route — 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist

### Unknown /api/v1 route — 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/does-not-exist

# --- Auth (Better Auth). Browser requests carry Origin; foreign origins get 403 INVALID_ORIGIN.
# The REST Client keeps the session cookie between requests.

### Sign in — 200 + httpOnly session cookie | 401 INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@tierra-andina.local", "password": "change-me-dev-only" }

### Current user and stores — 200 | 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me

### Current session (Better Auth) — 200, body null when signed out
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session

### Sign out — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-out
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Sign up is disabled — 400 EMAIL_PASSWORD_SIGN_UP_DISABLED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nadie", "email": "nadie@test.local", "password": "password-123" }

# --- Products (docs/modules/products.md §5). Sign in first (request above).
# Reads: any role (receivers get only id, name, saleUnit). Writes: owner only.
# Errors: 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND · 409 PRODUCT_NAME_TAKEN · 409 PRODUCT_UNITS_LOCKED ·
#         422 INVALID_UNIT_COMBINATION · 422 INVALID_PRODUCT_DEFAULTS · 422 CATEGORY_NOT_FOUND

### Categories — 200 { data: [{ id, code, name, sortOrder }] }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/product-categories

### List — 200 { data, total, page, pageSize }; search ignores case and accents
### sort: name | category | updated, "-" prefix for descending (default name)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?search=tomate&isActive=true&sort=-category&page=1&pageSize=20

### Create — 201 product (decimals as 4-decimal strings; lastMargin omitted → store default)
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tomate perita",
  "categoryId": "<id of the 'vegetable' category>",
  "purchaseUnit": "crate",
  "saleUnit": "kg",
  "defaultPackQuantity": "24",
  "lastShrinkage": "2",
  "lastMargin": "0.5"
}

### Quick create (purchase screen) — 201; category "other", shrinkage 0, default margin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/quick
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cilantro", "purchaseUnit": "bundle", "saleUnit": "unit", "defaultPackQuantity": "28" }

### Detail — 200 product + isUnitLocked
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}

### Update — 200; units rejected with 409 once the product is used
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lastMargin": "0.6" }

### Deactivate (soft delete) — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}/deactivate
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Activate — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}/activate
Origin: http://localhost:3000

# --- Settings and daily rates
### Store settings — 200 { usdRoundingStep, bsRoundingStep, saleRateMode, saleRateMarkupPct, defaultMargin, receiverCanSeePrices }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings

### Update settings (owner) — 200 all settings
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "defaultMargin": "0.5" }

### Set the day's rates (owner): BCV (global), Coche (market) and sale — 200 { businessDate, bcv, market, sale }
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exchange-rates/2026-10-19
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bcv": "200", "market": "201" }

### One day's rates (null when not set)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exchange-rates/2026-10-19

### Days with rates in a range (≤ 62 days), newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exchange-rates?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31

# --- Suppliers and purchases (owner). Errors: 404 TRIP_NOT_FOUND · 409 TRIP_CLOSED ·
#     422 DAY_RATES_MISSING · 404 LINE_NOT_FOUND · 422 LINE_PRODUCT_INVALID ·
#     422 SUPPLIER_NOT_FOUND · 422 INVALID_PURCHASE_LINE

### Suppliers — 200 { data }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers

### Create a supplier — 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/suppliers
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Puesto de Juan", "stallReference": "Nave 3, puesto 7" }

### Open a trip — 201; copies the day's BCV and Coche rates (422 DAY_RATES_MISSING if not set)
# @name openTrip
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "businessDate": "2026-10-19", "note": "Lunes" }

### Trips — 200 { data, total, page, pageSize }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips?status=open

### Add a line — 201 trip with lines. quotedPriceUsd is the line TOTAL; supplierRate defaults to
### the trip's Coche rate and margin to the product's last margin.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}/lines
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "<product id>",
  "stallReference": "Puesto 14",
  "packs": "3",
  "grossQuantity": "72",
  "shrinkage": "6",
  "quotedPriceUsd": "60",
  "paymentStatus": "paid"
}

### Trip with lines
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}

### Truck receipt (owner or receiver) — 200 the trip as the receiver sees it (prices hidden
### for receivers unless receiverCanSeePrices). status: received | partial | missing | pending
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}/lines/<line id>/receipt
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "partial", "receivedPacks": "2", "receivedQuantity": "47.5", "note": "Faltó una cesta" }

### Open trips with what to check at the truck — 200 { data: [{ id, businessDate, note, lines }] }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/receipts

### Close the trip — 200; lines can no longer change. Publishes the sale price list
### (422 SALE_RATE_MISSING if that day has no sale rate).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/purchase-trips/{{openTrip.response.body.id}}/close
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### What the shop still needs before Coche — 200 { data: [...] }, oldest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shopping-list

### Add a missing product — 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shopping-list
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "<product uuid>", "note": "se acabó" }

### Drop an open request — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shopping-list/<item id>/drop
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Sale prices in force (owner or manager) — 200, or 404 PRICE_LIST_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/price-lists/current
